usage: autonomous_software_controller.py [-h] --case CASE --run-root RUN_ROOT
                                         --contract CONTRACT --mandate MANDATE
                                         --native-image NATIVE_IMAGE
                                         --test-image TEST_IMAGE
                                         --public-catalog PUBLIC_CATALOG
                                         [--source-root SOURCE_ROOT]
                                         [--author-provider {codex,gemini}]
                                         [--author-model AUTHOR_MODEL]
                                         [--reviewer-provider {codex,gemini}]
                                         [--reviewer-model REVIEWER_MODEL]
                                         [--codex-volume CODEX_VOLUME]
                                         [--gemini-profile GEMINI_PROFILE]
                                         [--gemini-executable GEMINI_EXECUTABLE]
                                         [--seccomp SECCOMP] [--steps STEPS]

Explicit external Docker controller. Original provider profiles stay in place.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --case CASE           Existing local case; never recreated on resume
  --run-root RUN_ROOT   Private persistent host directory, outside provider
                        mounts
  --contract CONTRACT   Public delivery contract saved before generation
  --mandate MANDATE     Existing owner mandate; no new consent is inferred
  --native-image NATIVE_IMAGE
                        Inspected immutable sha256 image ID
  --test-image TEST_IMAGE
                        Inspected immutable sha256 image ID
  --public-catalog PUBLIC_CATALOG
                        Public pinned CLI model metadata; not profile data
  --source-root SOURCE_ROOT
  --author-provider {codex,gemini}
  --author-model AUTHOR_MODEL
  --reviewer-provider {codex,gemini}
  --reviewer-model REVIEWER_MODEL
  --codex-volume CODEX_VOLUME
  --gemini-profile GEMINI_PROFILE
  --gemini-executable GEMINI_EXECUTABLE
  --seccomp SECCOMP
  --steps STEPS         Explicit bounded dispatch count, maximum80
